// Resilience without I/O: circuit breaking, rate limiting, adaptive load shedding,
// backoff, rolling windows and deadlines.
//
// Every decision is a function of what the caller passes in. The clock is read by
// the caller, in nanoseconds, and so is the randomness a breaker's roll or a
// backoff's jitter needs, which is what makes every sequence here reproducible in
// a test. Policy numbers are parameters, each with a preset that is a reasonable
// place to start.
//
// Five jitter strategies ship: rigid, full, equal, decorrelated and spread. The
// first four are the shapes usually compared against each other; the last keeps a
// wait within a fraction of the ceiling, which is the one to reach for when the
// schedule is fixed.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moondate",
}
